    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter the July 3rd slate with a high-ceiling lineup led by **Yordan Alvarez** (86.62) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.13). **Yordan Alvarez** is the clear statistical anchor today; facing a mediocre matchup against Martinez, his elite 0.477 xwOBA combined with a positive platoon split and batting order boost makes him our primary offensive engine. Meanwhile, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is a high-leverage start for our team strategy; beyond his favorable platoon edge against Pallante, his ability to exploit the opposing pitcher\u2019s slow delivery reinforces his elite status in a category as scarce as stolen bases. **Junior Caminero** (74.38) and **Christian Yelich** (74.32) also project as high-efficiency starts, both benefiting from dynamic platoon advantages that elevate them well into our recommended tier.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved leaving **Luke Raley** on the bench. With a score of 39.07, **Luke Raley** missed our mandatory 40.0 floor by the narrowest of margins, primarily due to the daunting task of facing an elite arm in Cease, whose 3.01 xERA neutralized the potential gains from **Luke Raley**\u2019s platoon edge. While **Gary Sanchez** (54.62) occupies a lower scoring tier, he remains in the lineup to maximize position flexibility, provided he confirms into the #7 spot as projected. We are monitoring lineup reports closely for **Gary Sanchez** and **Christian Yelich** to ensure their assumed batting positions hold, as any movement down the order would trigger a re-evaluation of their daily efficiency scores.",
